# Production worker environment profile (FORGE_ENV=prod).
#
# Copy to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/forge/envs/prod.env (usually
# ~/.config/forge/envs/prod.env) and chmod 600. run-worker.sh selects this
# file from the plist-declared FORGE_ENV (=prod), parses it line-by-line as
# KEY=VALUE, and NEVER shell-evaluates values (T0.7/G35) — no quoting needed,
# `&` in a DB URL is safe. No `export`, no comments on value lines.
#
# This file declares FORGE_ENV_TAG=prod; run-worker.sh refuses to start if the
# tag disagrees with the plist's FORGE_ENV. FORGE_PROD_ACK is DELIBERATELY
# ABSENT here: the production acknowledgement lives only in the launchd plist
# (and, for interactive use, the shell), never in a profile file — defense in
# depth, so sourcing a profile can never by itself grant production access.

# --- Environment tag (must equal the plist's FORGE_ENV=prod) ---
FORGE_ENV_TAG=prod

# --- Temporal ---
# Nothing to set. The server address (127.0.0.1:7243) and the namespace
# (`forge-prod`) are both derived from FORGE_ENV=prod by
# sax_platform.config.resolve_temporal_target — see
# sax-temporal/docs/namespaces.md.
#
# FORGE_TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE is retired: it no longer exists as a setting, and a
# line for it here would be silently ignored. FORGE_TEMPORAL_ADDRESS still
# exists but only as an override, and prod accepts no value other than its own
# server.
#
# `forge-prod` exists on :7243 (created 2026-07-30). No drain is owed: the
# legacy :7233 stack was discarded the same day, histories included.

# --- Application store (shared sax-datastores prod stack, :5442) ---
# forge's local instance is retired. Each project is a role owning its
# same-named database with PUBLIC connect revoked, so a dev URL that leaks into
# this file fails at auth rather than reading production. Note the database
# NAMES changed with the move: `forge` -> `forge_prod`, `pbook` -> `pbook_prod`.
# Port 5442, not the 5432 default: reaching production takes explicit intent.
# Passwords are delivered by the sax-datastores admin
# (`make prod-url PROJECT=forge` / `PROJECT=pbook`).
FORGE_DB_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://forge_prod:CHANGEME@localhost:5442/forge_prod
PBOOK_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://pbook_prod:CHANGEME@localhost:5442/pbook_prod

# --- LLM / OCR keys ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: required by the forge worker (and the pbook worker, if
# installed) — the Anthropic SDK reads it from the environment.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=CHANGEME
# MISTRAL_API_KEY: REQUIRED by the ocr worker (install.sh --with-ocr). It is
# read at startup and the worker fails fast if it is unset or empty. Leave it
# commented out when the ocr worker is not installed.
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=CHANGEME
# OPENAI_API_KEY: pbook embeddings (install.sh --with-pbook).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=CHANGEME

# --- Blobs (production: real S3; the instance role is gone, so boto3 uses
# --- your ~/.aws config or explicit keys here) ---
FORGE_OCR_S3_BUCKET=CHANGEME
# FORGE_OCR_S3_PREFIX=ocr/
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=CHANGEME
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=CHANGEME
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-2

# --- Offsite backups: NOT forge's job any more ---
# FORGE_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET is retired. Nightly per-database `pg_dump -Fc` of every
# database on the prod instance — forge_prod and pbook_prod included, since the
# list is enumerated live rather than configured — is run by sax-datastores
# (`make prod-backup`, scheduled by launchd, verified by `make
# prod-restore-check`). deploy/local-stack/backup-app-dbs.sh dumped from the
# forge-postgres container, which no longer exists; setting a bucket here would
# only make a dead script fail confusingly, or suggest a second backup exists.
# See sax-datastores/docs/backups.md.

# --- Logging / observability ---
FORGE_LOG_DIR=/Users/CHANGEME/.local/state/forge/logs
FORGE_OTEL_EXPORTER=none
# FORGE_OTEL_ENDPOINT is only read when FORGE_OTEL_EXPORTER is otlp_grpc/otlp_http.
# FORGE_OTEL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317
